	<item>
		<title><![CDATA[Why we moved our queue to Postgres]]></title>
		<link>https://blog.acme.io/2026/03/12/why-we-moved-our-queue-to-postgres/</link>
		<pubDate>Thu, 12 Mar 2026 16:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[sofia]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://blog.acme.io/?p=42</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[We ran our job queue on Redis for six years. In March we moved it to Postgres, next to the data the jobs change.

The reason is simple: a job and the row it updates now commit together.
Nothing is lost between them.

[caption id="attachment_41" align="aligncenter" width="1200"]<img class="size-full wp-image-41" src="https://blog.acme.io/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/queue-dashboard.png" alt="The queue dashboard after the move" width="1200" height="675" /> Jobs per second, the week of the move.[/caption]

https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQw4w9WgXcQ

<!--more-->

<h2>What we kept</h2>
<ul>
	<li>The retry schedule</li>
	<li>The dead letter queue</li>
</ul>

[gallery ids="43,44,45"]

Questions? Write to {{ reply_to }} and we'll answer in the next post.]]></content:encoded>
		<excerpt:encoded><![CDATA[<p>A job and the row it updates now commit together.</p>]]></excerpt:encoded>
